On February 14, 2023, the [[FIFA Council]] approved the slot allocation for the 2025 tournament based on a "set of objective metrics and criteria". [[UEFA]] was awarded the most slots with twelve, while [[CONMEBOL]] was given the second most with six. The [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]], [[Confederation of African Football|CAF]], and [[CONCACAF]] were all given four slots, while the [[Oceania Football Confederation|OFC]] and the host association were given one slot each.<ref name="slots">{{cite news |url=https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/fifa-council-highlights-record-breaking-revenue-in-football |title=FIFA Council highlights record breaking revenue in football |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com|date=February 14, 2023 |access-date=February 14, 2023 |archive-date=February 14, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230214163245/https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/fifa-council-highlights-record-breaking-revenue-in-football |url-status=live }}</ref> On March 14, 2023, the FIFA Council approved the key principles of the access list for the tournament.<ref name="access list">{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/fifa-council-approves-international-match-calendars |title=FIFA Council approves international match calendars |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com |date=March 14, 2023 |access-date=March 14, 2023 |archive-date=March 14, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230314155521/https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/fifa-council/media-releases/fifa-council-approves-international-match-calendars |url-status=live }}</ref> The principles were as follows, considering competitions completed during a four-year period from 2021 to 2024:<ref name="rankings">{{cite web |title=FIFA Club World Cup 2025™ Confederations ranking |url=https://inside.fifa.com/fifa-rankings/fifa-club-world-cup |access-date=June 13, 2024 |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com|archive-date=June 21, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240621032232/https://inside.fifa.com/fifa-rankings/fifa-club-world-cup |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[CONMEBOL]] and [[UEFA]] (more than four slots): access for the winners of the confederation's top club competition between 2021 and 2024, with additional teams to be determined by a club ranking of the four-year period.<ref name="rankings"/>
* [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]], [[Confederation of African Football|CAF]], and [[CONCACAF]] (four slots each): access for the winners of the confederation's top club competition between 2021 and 2024.<ref name="rankings"/>{{refn|group=note|name=AFC slot|As the [[AFC Champions League]] was shifted from an intra-year schedule to an inter-year schedule starting from 2023–24, only three seasons of the AFC Champions League were completed within the 2021 to 2024 timeframe, resulting in the remaining slot allocated using the four-year club ranking.<ref name="rankings"/>}}
* [[Oceania Football Confederation|OFC]] (one slot): access for the highest-ranked club among the winners of the confederation's top club competition between 2021 and 2024.<ref name="rankings"/>{{refn|group=note|name=OFC|As the [[2021 OFC Champions League]] was canceled, the slot was awarded to the best club in the OFC's four-year ranking that won the competition between 2022 and 2024.<ref name="rankings"/><ref>{{cite news |title=City confirmed for expanded 2025 Club World Cup |url=http://www.aucklandcityfc.com/news/2164/12/City-confirmed-for-expanded-2025-Club-World-Cup/ |access-date=March 18, 2024 |publisher=Auckland City FC |archive-date=August 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240829100158/http://www.aucklandcityfc.com/news/2164/12/City-confirmed-for-expanded-2025-Club-World-Cup/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=December 18, 2023 |title=Auckland City qualify for revamped FIFA Club World Cup to be held in 2025 |url=https://www.friendsoffootballnz.com/2023/12/18/auckland-city-qualify-for-revamped-fifa-club-world-cup-to-be-held-in-2025/ |access-date=March 18, 2024 |website=Friends of Football}}</ref>}}
* Host country (one slot): this was determined at a later stage.

If a club won two or more seasons of its confederation's top club competition, additional teams determined club rankings over the four-year period. Furthermore, a restriction of two clubs per association was applied, with the exception of champion clubs if more than two clubs from the same association won their confederation's top club competition. The calculation method for the four-year club rankings within each confederation was based on the teams' performance in their respective continental tournaments during seasons completed between 2021 and 2024.<ref name="method">{{cite web |title=FIFA Club World Cup 2025: How teams qualify |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/how-teams-qualify |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com |access-date=October 7, 2024 |date=August 19, 2024 |archive-date=October 7, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241007104244/https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/how-teams-qualify |url-status=live }}</ref>

For confederations other than UEFA, the method was as follows:<ref name="method"/>
* 3 points for a win
* 1 point for a draw
* 3 points for successful progression to each new stage of the competition

In the case of UEFA, due to the existence of the well-established [[UEFA coefficient#Men's club coefficient|UEFA club coefficient]] system, the method used by UEFA to calculate the club coefficient was "exceptionally applied" to rank the European teams.<ref name="method"/>{{refn|group=note|name=UEFA coefficient|However, the system was only applied over the four years, instead of the usual five, to the Champions League exclusively.}}
{{clear}}

