==Venues==

On September 28, 2024, FIFA announced the selection of twelve venues in eleven cities for the tournament: [[Lincoln Financial Field]] in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; [[Audi Field]] in Washington D.C.; [[Lumen Field]] in Seattle, Washington; the [[Rose Bowl (stadium)|Rose Bowl]] in Pasadena, California; [[TQL Stadium]] in Cincinnati, Ohio; [[Bank of America Stadium]] in Charlotte, North Carolina; [[Mercedes-Benz Stadium]] in Atlanta, Georgia; [[Hard Rock Stadium]] in Miami Gardens, Florida, which hosted the opening match involving Inter Miami;<ref name="miami qual">{{cite news |date=October 19, 2024 |title=Inter Miami CF joins FIFA Club World Cup 2025™ line-up following 2024 MLS Supporters' Shield success |url=https://inside.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/media-releases/inter-miami-cf-joins-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-tm-line-up-mls-supporters-shield |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241111205039/https://inside.fifa.com/about-fifa/organisation/media-releases/inter-miami-cf-joins-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-tm-line-up-mls-supporters-shield |archive-date=November 11, 2024 |access-date=October 20, 2024 |publisher=[[FIFA]]}}</ref> [[Geodis Park]] in Nashville, Tennessee; [[Camping World Stadium]] and [[Inter&Co Stadium]] in Orlando, Florida; and [[MetLife Stadium]] in East Rutherford, New Jersey, which hosted the [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup final|final]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cardenas |first=Felipe |title=FIFA announces 2025 Club World Cup stadiums and cities |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5798811/2024/09/28/club-world-cup-2025-venues/ |access-date=September 28, 2024 |work=The Athletic |archive-date=September 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240929001157/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5798811/2024/09/28/club-world-cup-2025-venues/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Lumen Field hosted all three group stage matches for the Seattle Sounders.<ref name="Seattle Times">{{cite news |last=Evans |first=Jayda |date=September 28, 2024 |title=FIFA announces Lumen Field as Club World Cup 2025 venue |url=https://www.seattletimes.com/sports/sounders/fifa-announces-lumen-field-as-club-world-cup-2025-venue/ |work=The Seattle Times |access-date=September 28, 2024 |archive-date=September 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240929003635/https://www.seattletimes.com/sports/sounders/fifa-announces-lumen-field-as-club-world-cup-2025-venue/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Of these selected stadiums, five were used in the following summer's [[2026 FIFA World Cup|World Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Jones |first=J. Sam |date=June 16, 2022 |title=Your guide to 2026 World Cup stadiums and locations in the US, Mexico and Canada |url=https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/your-guide-to-the-2026-world-cup-stadiums-and-locations-in-the-us-mexico-and-can |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221107072054/https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/your-guide-to-the-2026-world-cup-stadiums-and-locations-in-the-us-mexico-and-can |archive-date=November 7, 2022 |access-date=November 6, 2022 |work=MLSsoccer.com}}</ref> Unlike other FIFA tournaments, including the 2026 FIFA World Cup, all venues kept their original [[naming rights]].<ref>{{cite web |title=FIFA names 12 stadiums set to stage historic FIFA Club World Cup 2025™ |url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/fifa-names-12-stadiums-set-to-stage-historic-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-tm |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250318061722/https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/fifa-names-12-stadiums-set-to-stage-historic-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-tm |archive-date=March 18, 2025 |access-date=April 4, 2025 |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |url-status=live }}</ref>{{Clear}}

