===Training bases===
According to a report from ''[[The Athletic]]'', FIFA designated sites in host cities for team training bases, with priority given to clubs that had more matches in the area. Clubs were permitted to independently negotiate with other facility owners and operators, including several college athletic programs, to secure their own base. Several facilities were also designated by FIFA for use later in the tournament by qualified teams in the knockout rounds.<ref>{{cite news |last=Crafton |first=Adam |date=March 12, 2025 |title=FIFA, the Club World Cup and the scrap for US training bases among major clubs |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6195796/2025/03/12/fifa-club-world-cup-training-bases-usa-clubs/ |work=The Athletic |url-access=subscription |accessdate=March 12, 2025 |archive-date=March 16, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316152324/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6195796/2025/03/12/fifa-club-world-cup-training-bases-usa-clubs/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The team base camps for the group stage were confirmed by FIFA on June 3, 2025.<ref name="basecamps">{{cite press release |date=June 3, 2025 |title=The world's best football talents set to be welcomed by communities across the United States |url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/club-world-cup-team-base-camp-training-sites-confirmed |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com |accessdate=June 3, 2025}}</ref>

