==Schedule==
On December 17, 2023, FIFA announced the tournament would take place from June 15 to July 13, 2025.<ref name="key details"/> Prior to the draw, only the date and venue of the opening match (involving [[Inter Miami CF|Inter Miami]]) and final was confirmed, along with the venue for the group stage matches of the [[Seattle Sounders FC|Seattle Sounders]]. The full match schedule with venues and kickoff times was finalized and published on December 7, 2024, following the draw.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/match-schedule-announced|title=FIFA Club World Cup 2025™: Match schedule released|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com |access-date=December 7, 2024|archive-date=December 7, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207091505/https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/match-schedule-announced|url-status=live}}</ref> The start date of the tournament was altered, with the tournament beginning one day earlier on June 14. The schedule was created taking into account factors such as "sporting and player-centric criteria, local and traveling fans and global broadcast considerations".<ref name="procedures confirmed"/>

==Squads==
{{Main|2025 FIFA Club World Cup squads}}

Each club was required to name a provisional squad of between 26 and 50 players for the tournament. From June 1 to 10, 2025, the member associations of all participating clubs implemented an extraordinary transfer window to allow for the registration of newly signed players. Clubs were required to name their final squads of between 26 and 35 players, including at least three goalkeepers, by June 10.<ref name="groundbreaking">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/groundbreaking-transfer-window-club-world-cup-32-teams-sign-new-players |title=Groundbreaking transfer window to allow all 32 FIFA Club World Cup teams to sign new players for the tournament |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |date=May 21, 2025 |access-date=June 3, 2025 |archive-date=June 11, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250611082001/https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/media-releases/groundbreaking-transfer-window-club-world-cup-32-teams-sign-new-players |url-status=live }}</ref> During the competition, clubs could make [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup squads#Player eligibility and transfer rules|limited changes]] to their final lists from June 27 to July 3, should the club's member association have a transfer window open during this period, though no player could appear for two clubs during the tournament.<ref name="FAQ">{{cite web |url=https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/1816f97fa21bfde0/original/FIFA-Club-World-Cup-2025-FAQ-General-Regulatory-Matters_EN.pdf |title=General Regulatory Matters FIFA Club World Cup 2025 |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |date=May 21, 2025 |access-date=June 3, 2025 |archive-date=June 3, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250603114546/https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/1816f97fa21bfde0/original/FIFA-Club-World-Cup-2025-FAQ-General-Regulatory-Matters_EN.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref> Should a club's [[Goalkeeper (association football)|goalkeeper]] have suffered from an injury or illness, that player could be replaced at any time.<ref name="regulations"/>

==Opening ceremony==
[[French Montana]] and [[Swae Lee]] headlined the opening ceremony, which took place at [[Miami]]'s [[Hard Rock Stadium]] before the opening match between [[Al Ahly SC|Al Ahly]] and [[Inter Miami CF|Inter Miami]]. Singers Vikina and Richaelio also performed during the ceremony, which was broadcast on [[DAZN]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.si.com/soccer/fifa-announce-2025-club-world-cup-opening-ceremony-headline-acts|title=FIFA announces the 2025 Club World Cup headlines acts|publisher=Sports Illustrated|date=June 5, 2025|access-date=June 10, 2025|archive-date=June 10, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250610073217/https://www.si.com/soccer/fifa-announce-2025-club-world-cup-opening-ceremony-headline-acts|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Group stage==
In the group stage, teams were divided into eight groups of four (groups A to H). Teams in each group played one another in a [[round-robin tournament|round-robin]], from which the top two teams advanced to the [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup knockout stage|knockout stage]].

