==Marketing==

===Branding===
On September 4, 2024, FIFA released the official emblem and audio signature of the tournament. The emblem took inspiration from the ball, football history and culture, with the initials of the tournament abstracted into a circular icon.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/emblem-audio-signature-revealed|title=FIFA unveils emblem and audio signature for new FIFA Club World Cup|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com|date=September 4, 2024}}</ref> The official audio featured Italian singer [[Gala (singer)|Gala]]'s song "[[Freed from Desire]]".<ref>{{cite web |date=September 4, 2024 |title=FIFA unveil Club World Cup logo and official audio with help from DJ Khaled |url=https://en.as.com/soccer/fifa-unveil-club-world-cup-logo-and-official-audio-with-help-from-dj-khaled-n/ |access-date=September 6, 2024 |website=AS |archive-date=September 10, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240910085250/https://en.as.com/soccer/fifa-unveil-club-world-cup-logo-and-official-audio-with-help-from-dj-khaled-n/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On November 14, FIFA unveiled the new Club World Cup trophy.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Robson |first1=James |title=FIFA unveils NASA-inspired golden Club World Cup trophy created with Tiffany & Co. |url=https://ca.sports.yahoo.com/news/fifa-unveils-nasa-inspired-golden-191102956.html |website=Yahoo Sports |access-date=November 15, 2024 |date=November 14, 2024 |archive-date=December 2, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241202231448/https://ca.sports.yahoo.com/news/fifa-unveils-nasa-inspired-golden-191102956.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Innovative FIFA Club World Cup Trophy unveiled ahead of new tournament in 2025 |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/innovative-trophy-unveiled |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com |access-date=November 15, 2024 |date=November 14, 2024 |archive-date=November 14, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241114223329/https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/innovative-trophy-unveiled |url-status=live }}</ref> On January 29, 2025, it was announced that FIFA Music Ambassador [[Robbie Williams]] would perform at the tournament, including a new song.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/news/origin1904-p.cxm.fifa.com/robbie-williams-music-ambassador-club-world-cup-2025-song|date=January 29, 2025|title=Pop superstar Robbie Williams to collaborate with FIFA on various music projects as FIFA Music Ambassador|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com}}</ref>

===Match ball===
On January 31, 2025, the official match ball was revealed by [[Adidas]]. The design featured jagged-edged block patterns and deconstructed stars and stripes in red, white, and blue, the colors of the [[flag of the United States]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://inside.fifa.com/organisation/news/club-world-cup-2025-adidas-official-match-ball-unveiled|title=FIFA Club World Cup 2025™ Official Match Ball unveiled by adidas|date=January 31, 2025|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com|accessdate=January 31, 2025}}</ref> On July 7, the official match ball for the final was revealed. It featured the same design as the previous ball, but the red part was switched to gold. The ball was used for the tournament's last three matches: both semi-finals and the final, all of which were held at the [[MetLife Stadium]] in East Rutherford.<ref>{{cite news|first=Ash|last=Rose|url=https://www.dazn.com/en-GB/news/football/adidas-reveal-matchball-for-the-fifa-club-world-cup-semi-finals-cwc25uk/kqppyjfiyncz1nm8npn3ntxfc|title=Adidas reveal matchball for the FIFA Club World Cup semi-finals|date=July 7, 2025|website=DAZN|access-date=July 7, 2025|archive-date=July 8, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250708044145/https://www.dazn.com/en-GB/news/football/adidas-reveal-matchball-for-the-fifa-club-world-cup-semi-finals-cwc25uk/kqppyjfiyncz1nm8npn3ntxfc|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Music===
Alongside Gala's "Freed from Desire", a remake of the [[Queen (band)|Queen]] song "[[We Will Rock You]]" by American rapper [[Pitbull (rapper)|Pitbull]] and producer [[RedOne]] served as one of the official songs of the tournament. Pitbull sang the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]] official song, "[[We Are One (Ole Ola)]]", while RedOne produced the [[2022 FIFA World Cup|2022 tournament]]'s [[FIFA World Cup Qatar 2022 Official Soundtrack|official album]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/club-world-cup/usa-2025/articles/pitbull-redone-official-song-we-will-rock-you|title=Pitbull and RedOne reimagine We Will Rock You as Official Song|date=June 14, 2025|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association|website=FIFA.com|accessdate=July 7, 2025}}</ref> The TV title sequence used a remix of "Freed from Desire" released by [[Diplo]] the previous year.

The listening of "Freed from Desire" exploded during the tournament, with various [[Internet meme]]s using the song being made in various [[social media]] platforms and [[Spotify]] announcing a rise of over 13% in daily average listening globally during late June 2025, including a boost YoY in some regions; as an example, in Brazil, the song had a rise of over 850% vs. the same period in 2024 and a 450% rise just in the first half of June 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last=Souza |first=Adrielly |date=July 3, 2025 |title=Nananana...: 'Freed From Desire' vira hino na Copa e dispara mais de 850% no Spotify |trans-title='Freed From Desire' becomes a trend in the CWC and gets over 800% boost in Spotify |url=https://f5.folha.uol.com.br/musica/2025/07/freed-from-desire-vira-hino-das-arquibancadas-e-dispara-mais-de-850-no-spotify.shtml |access-date=July 4, 2025 |website=F5 |publisher=[[Folha de S.Paulo]] |language=pt-BR}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=July 3, 2025 |title=Trilha da Copa do Mundo de Clubes explode no Spotify com crescimento de 854% no Brasil |trans-title=Club World Cup theme explodes on Spotify with a 854% boost in Brazil |url=https://maquinadoesporte.com.br/futebol/trilha-da-copa-do-mundo-de-clubes-explode-no-spotify-com-crescimento-de-854-no-brasil/ |access-date=July 4, 2025 |website=Máquina do Esporte |language=pt-BR |archive-date=July 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250704100625/https://maquinadoesporte.com.br/futebol/trilha-da-copa-do-mundo-de-clubes-explode-no-spotify-com-crescimento-de-854-no-brasil/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title='Fear from Desire': o hit dos anos 90 que virou febre na Copa do Mundo de Clubes 2025 |url=https://exame.com/pop/fear-from-desire-o-hit-dos-anos-90-que-virou-febre-na-copa-do-mundo-de-clubes-2025/ |access-date=July 4, 2025 |date=July 3, 2025 |website=Exame |language=pt-br}}</ref>

